==English==
{{Wikiquote}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar|en}} {{term|حديث|tr=ħadí:θ|lang=ar||Prophetic tradition}}, from {{term|حدث|tr=ħáddaθa|lang=ar||to tell, relate, report}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|hadiːθ|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|ha|dith|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|hadith|hadiths|ahadith}}

# {{context|countable|religion|Islam}} An [[eyewitness]] [[account]] of a [[saying]] or [[action]] of [[Muhammad]] (or [[sometimes]] one of his [[companion]]s) not [[otherwise]] [[found]] in the [[Quran]].
#: ''There are four main Shia books of '''hadith''' and six main Sunni books of '''hadith'''.''
#: ''In addition to the Qur'an, many Muslims also look to the '''hadiths''' for moral and spiritual guidance in their daily lives.''
# {{context|uncountable|religion|Islam|usually|_|capitalized}} The [[entire]] [[body]] of [[such]] [[account]]s.
#: ''The '''Hadith''' are believed to be the words of the Prophet, memorized by his followers and written down in the first or second centuries after the Hegira.''
# {{context|countable|religion|Islam}} A [[particular]] [[accepted]] [[collection]] of [[such]] [[account]]s, as from a [[single]] [[source]] or within a [[particular]] [[branch]] of [[Islam]] or [[Islam]]ic [[jurisprudence]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|uncountable}} the [[Hadith]], [[tradition]]
* {{sense|countable}} [[saying]], [[deed]], etc.

====Related terms====
* [[Sunna]]
